+## Findings, ranked
+
+### FINDING #1 — INTEGRATION_MISMATCH · **blocks DONE** · new, not one of review-1's five
+
+**The resolver's own output slice is rejected as malformed by every external worker. A SCOPED job
+with an unmapped changed path cannot be dispatched to Codex, Antigravity, Cursor, opencode or
+Devin — the worker dies at usage-fault exit 2 before the model runs.**
+
+Two independent causes, both in the same slice:
+
+| Cause | Producer | Consumer that rejects it |
+|---|---|---|
+| `scope: "impacted+referencing"` | `scripts/compound-v-fastpath-run.py:891` (`scope_label`) | `scripts/compound-v-run-codex-worker.sh:131` — `.scope as $s \| ["full","impacted","floor_only"] \| index($s) != null` |
+| the extra key `selected_count` | `scripts/compound-v-fastpath-run.py:929-930` | `scripts/compound-v-run-codex-worker.sh:129` — `((keys) - ["scope","floor_command","full_command","resolved_commands"]) \| length == 0` |
+
+The same guard is duplicated verbatim in `compound-v-run-antigravity-worker.sh:138`,
+`compound-v-run-cursor-worker.sh:145`, `compound-v-run-opencode-worker.sh:179` and
+`compound-v-run-devin-worker.sh:158`.
+
+The two ends are wired directly together: `compound-v-emit-workflow.py:2662-2676` writes the
+slice by calling `resolve-tests --out <path>` and returns that same path, which
+`:1335-1336` then passes as `--test-contract-file`. Nothing normalises the label or strips the
+key in between.
+
+**Reproduced**, on a sandbox repo with an unmapped changed path at `triage.tier: SCOPED`:
+
+```bash
+compound-v-fastpath-run.py resolve-tests --worktree "$WT" --baseline "$B" \
+  --manifest "$M" --job-id j1 --no-prior-run --out slice.json
+```
+```json
+{"scope": "impacted+referencing",
+ "resolved_commands": ["sh -c 'echo floor'", "python3 tests/test_ref1.py", …],
+ "selected_count": 6, "floor_command": "…", "full_command": "…"}
+```
+```bash
+jq -e '(((keys) - ["scope","floor_command","full_command","resolved_commands"]) | length) == 0
+       and (.scope as $s | ["full","impacted","floor_only"] | index($s) != null)' slice.json
+# guard exit=1     → tc_validate() calls die "--test-contract-file is malformed"
+```
+
+This is **not** introduced by `e9ab86f`. Both the label and `selected_count` came from the 3.4.1
+decision-4 jobs and landed in r3. Review-1 verified the slice by reading its JSON and never handed
+it to the thing that consumes it, which is exactly the seam PASS 3 exists to check. It is invisible
+to every criterion because this repository dispatches Claude jobs, which do not go through
+`tc_validate`.
+
+The `job_result` schema note in the reviewer contract ("the resolved *slice* additionally carries
+the output-only label `impacted+referencing`") documents the producer's side. The five worker
+scripts document the consumer's, and they disagree.
+
+→ Pick one contract and make both ends obey it. Either the workers' guard accepts
+`impacted+referencing` and an optional `selected_count`, or the emitted `--test-contract-file`
+carries the three-value label with the extra detail in the notes. Do not fix it by deleting the
+guard — it is the check that stops a blank or empty command set becoming a fabricated pass.
+
