+### FINDING #4 — QUALITY, low (review-1 issue #4, **partially closed**)
+
+**The label follows the obligation on the unmapped branch and not on its sibling. A slice that
+pulled in `full_command` through the previously-failing fallback still says `impacted`.**
+
+The fix is correct where review-1 pointed:
+
+```
+tier=FULL, unmapped path src/widget.go
+  "scope": "full"
+  "resolved_commands": ["sh -c 'echo floor'", "sh -c 'echo FULLSUITE'"]
+  note: "scope: labelled `full` — full_command was added for an unmapped path at this tier"
+```
+
+But `resolve_test_commands` appends `full_command` from **two** places, and only one relabels.
+The other is `scripts/compound-v-fastpath-run.py:864-868` — the previously-failing set is
+uncomputable, so the floor falls back to the whole suite. Reproduced at tier SCOPED with a
+`last_result` carrying no `tests.failures[]`:
+
+```json
+{"scope": "impacted+referencing",
+ "resolved_commands": ["sh -c 'echo floor'", "sh -c 'echo FULLSUITE'",
+                       "python3 tests/test_ref1.py", … ],
+ "selected_count": 7}
+```
+```
+note: "previously-failing: UNCOMPUTABLE … falling back to full_command rather than silently
+       dropping the set"
+note: "unmapped: src/widget.py … resolves to the 5 test(s) REFERENCING the changed module(s),
+       NOT to full_command (v3.4.1 decision 4; capped at 5)"
+```
+
+`full_command` is in the set; one note says it was added and the other says it was not; the label
+says neither. This over-runs rather than under-runs, so nothing goes untested — but it is the same
+reviewer-facing contradiction issue #4 named, in the branch the fix did not reach, and it now
+makes the two notes in a single slice disagree with each other.
